Because this loads the post in order to modify it, the entity must be tracked, so it isn't a read-only query. I used query syntax, a `var` query run in a separate awaited statement, and a `CancellationToken`.

```csharp
public static async Task RenamePostAsync(
    BlogContext blogContext,
    int postId,
    string newTitle,
    CancellationToken cancellationToken)
{
    var postQuery =
        from post in blogContext.Posts
        where post.Id == postId
        select post;

    var matchingPost = await postQuery.SingleOrDefaultAsync(cancellationToken);

    if (matchingPost is null)
    {
        throw new InvalidOperationException($"Post {postId} was not found.");
    }

    matchingPost.Title = newTitle;

    await blogContext.SaveChangesAsync(cancellationToken);
}
